Well, no one has chimed in yet, so I'll give it a shot.

I see your logic, and I like your continual efforts to make the package neater, but my take would be to leave things as they are for consistency. I think it would be easier for new users to find that 
    DT[,c("colA","colB")]
and 
    colvars = c("colA","colB")
    DT[,colvars]  
both don't work, and realize they need to use with=FALSE, rather than finding that the two lead to different results.

Joe Voelkel


